1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Agent harnesses stop and wait for a human before anything irreversible.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
But the pause is buried in a chat transcript.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Run five agents and the approval that matters is three tabs deep.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:30,000
ApproveDeck is mission control for TrueForge approvals. One screen, every gate.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Each card: which agent, which tool, the exact payload, how long it waited.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Destructive tools glow red and require a 650 millisecond hold to arm.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
One hold, and the decision posts straight back into the TrueForge API.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The agent resumes immediately. The deck goes back to all clear.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
This run was real: 1,143 rows deleted in a live Postgres database.

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
With a verified rollback on file, and a full chain of custody.

11
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Built on TrueForge. For everyone running more agents than browser tabs.
